\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Initializes and returns an NSDateFormatter instance that uses the date \i format\i0  in its conversions. See the description of NSCalendarDate\'27s \b dateWithCalendarFormat:timeZone:\b0  for a list of conversion specifiers permitted in date format strings. Set \i flag\i0  to YES if you want the NSDateFormatter to process dates entered as expressions in the vernacular (for example, \'aatomorrow\'ba); NSDateFormatter attempts natural-language processing only after it fails to interpret an entered string according to \i format\i0 . The following example creates a date formatter with the format string (as example) \'aaMar 15 1994\'ba and then associates the formatter with the cells of a form (\b contactsForm\b0 ).\
\fs14\
